# Deviations from PROTOCOL_API.md (recorded as they happened)
- D1: the global endpoint answered 429 RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED for most calls; each run index moved to a regional endpoint (run 1 us-east4, run 2 europe-west4, run 3 us-east1), the same region for both arms of a run.
- D2: gemini-2.5-flash looped on one failing tool call past the 15-call limit, ignoring the text reminder. After 15 tool calls (or 3 text replies without a call) on a question, the harness now sets the API's function-calling mode to allow only submit_answer, which enforces the protocol's own limit. Every function call is logged. All six chains restarted from scratch under the same rules.
- D3: under sustained 429s the harness gave up after 8 retries and the chain's thread died (two chains stopped). The caller now moves to the next region in a fixed pool on any 429, 5xx or dropped connection (the same model, gemini-2.5-flash) and never gives up. The run restarted from scratch, since a CMLM chain carries taught state across its sessions.
- D4: all three Vertex runs stopped on HTTP 401: the harness kept a gcloud access token for 25 minutes, and gcloud can return a token near its expiry. Tokens are now refreshed every 5 minutes and on any 401. The question run restarted from scratch; the bug bash resumed (its sessions are independent); the Model D eyes run restarted.
- D5: the blind judge found non-answers ("I am waiting for the next question") in the CMLM arm (7 of 60 in run 1) and in Model D's one-question body sessions (31 of 120). The ranked code came before the question, and the one-question sessions reused the 10-question instructions. Fix, the same in every arm: the question first and the ranked code after; instructions that match the session length; a submitted non-answer gets the question repeated instead of being accepted. The CMLM arm (3 runs) and Model D's questions (3 runs) are rerun from scratch. ALONE had no non-answers and no readout, so it stands.
